#!/bin/bash
# land-budget-is-a-target.sh — the budget stops being only a ceiling.
#
# 90%–105% of what you set, per category, with compatibility and effectiveness
# still ranked above using the money. Where the shelf cannot reach the target,
# the plan says why instead of padding itself.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# PRECONDITION: land-routine-budget-ui.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="A budget is a target, not only a ceiling"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"A budget you cannot see being spent"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-routine-budget-ui.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="3e44101a2dd4fe8d9f8c5a3347ea742313ad35891ed2b9789ed1246463fc7233"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== gates: the API"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/beauty
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/beauty/budget-routine.ts \
        together-city-chat/src/beauty/budget-is-a-limit.spec.ts \
        together-city-react/src/features/beauty/api.ts \
        together-city-react/src/features/beauty/pages/Routine.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/app/budget-is-on-the-page.test.ts
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A budget is a target, not only a ceiling

A 5,000 face budget was answering with a 1,108 routine. Every rule was being
obeyed: never over, cheapest compatible product for every step, nothing added
that wasn't needed. Twenty-two per cent of what somebody had deliberately set
aside, with better-matched products for those very steps sitting unbought on
the shelf. "Never over" turns out to be half of a budget. The other half is
that the money was put there to be used.

So the objective is a range now, applied to face, hair and body separately:

  TARGET     B x 0.90 to B          as close to B as the shelf allows
  HEADROOM   up to B x 1.05         only for a meaningfully better match
  CEILING    B x 1.05               never crossed, for anything, ever

The ordering of objectives is written as control flow so utilisation cannot get
in front of suitability by accident: compatibility, then effectiveness, then
whether the step is needed at all, then using the budget, then value for money.
Budget utilisation is fourth of five. A compatible 3,200 routine beats an
incompatible 4,900 one, and there is now a test that fails if any step in a plan
is worse-matched than something available for the same step.

Reaching the target has exactly two honest instruments.

  A BETTER PRODUCT for a step already in the routine. The old comparator led
  with price, which is how the ties — and there are many, because two
  moisturisers for the same skin type score the same and should — all went to
  the cheaper bottle. It leads with how many of this person's findings the
  product answers now, and money breaks ties rather than deciding them.

  A PREMIUM ALTERNATIVE, and only while under target. The catalogue carries the
  sheet's own grade — Budget, Mid-range, Premium — and a real grade jump is the
  test, not a higher price: two mid-range moisturisers at 196 and 640 are the
  same idea in a bigger bottle. The candidate must never be less suitable, and
  the pass stops the instant the routine reaches 90%.

Two things that pass took to get right. Choosing whichever single swap landed
closest to the budget — the obvious greedy — put a 3,300-a-month sunscreen in a
5,000 routine: one enormous move hits the number faster than five sensible ones.
It climbs in the smallest available increments instead. And no step the target
passes reach for may exceed half the category budget, because a routine where
one product is most of the bill is a purchase with four accessories attached.

Where neither instrument can reach 90%, the plan stops and says so — every
compatible step already in, every step already holding the best product for it,
and the rest of the money buying nothing worth having. That sentence comes from
the planner rather than the page, because the planner is the only thing that
knows it is true.

Where the best compatible routine costs more than the ceiling allows, the figure
is offered and never taken: "the best routine we can build comes to 1,437/month,
above the 1,000 you set" — Set 1,437, or Keep 1,000. And on the rare occasion
the routine does use the five per cent headroom, the card says so in as many
words. A budget crossed silently is a budget that was only ever advisory.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: A budget is a target, not only a ceiling
 Both sides — push, then give Railway a minute to redeploy
 before reloading the routine.
===============================================================

DONE
